      "statement": "Calculated activation-state comparisons support oxidation of neutral 2a rather than substrate reduction or triplet energy transfer under the supplied catalyst conditions.",
      "expected": "Recover the author-supported energetic discrimination using actual computations and explicit state/electrode/solvent definitions. SI9.1 reports Eox(2a)=+1.10 V and Ered(2a)=-2.69 V versus SCE in MeCN, using the neutral singlet, +1 doublet and -1 doublet of the complete 65-atom substrate. Compare on a compatible scale with the supplied catalyst data, preserving the MeCN/DCM distinction; exact DCM SET free energies are not author results. SI9.2 supports a substrate triplet requirement above the reported PC A/B triplet energies, disfavouring triplet energy transfer. The exact substrate triplet target is source-conflicted (main73.9 versus SI74.1 kcal/mol) and is not a numerical scoring requirement. Assess only the robust energetic ordering after verifying the submitter's definition and actual evidence. Redox values have no calibrated new tolerance: manual scientific comparison, no invented acceptance window. Merely repeating the public catalyst screen or proposing a radical cation without quantitative discriminating evidence earns no activation result credit. Do not require explicit PC-substrate SET TSs, transfer rates, counterion energetics or a complete cycle. Supported portions may earn partial credit; an unresolved calculation does not establish the corresponding finding.",
