      "expected": "Recover the neutral 2a and neutral 3a identities (C26H36BNSi, 65 atoms, charge0 singlets), together with the computed rearranged +1 doublet Int2 having C4-product connectivity. Source Int2 lies at -37.4 kcal/mol on the radical-cation profile; this contextual value has no new numeric window. Int2 + e- -> 3a conserves all atoms, without a required proton transfer or loss. Link actual computed endpoint graphs/states to the neutral-start interpretation, not bookkeeping alone. For supplied catalyst B, consistent stoichiometric accounting is PC(+1)* + 2a -> PC(0) + [2a](+1), then PC(0) + [3a](+1) -> PC(+1) + 3a; PF6- is unchanged. These catalyst statements are electron bookkeeping for the author-proposed mechanism, not computed SET kinetics or an independently proven catalytic cycle. Do not require or score an absolute cross-charge reduction free energy, the plotted -170.8 endpoint as a reaction energy, or an electron-transfer TS.",
